<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36813" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pŏētĭcus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποιητικός</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>poetic</i>, <i>poetical</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">verbum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. de Or. 3, 38, 153</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">non poëtico sed quodam oratorio numero
					et modo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 1, 33, 151</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">di,</span>”
				<i>represented by the poets</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					N. D. 3, 31, 151</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quadrigae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Q. Fr. 2, 15, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mella,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor. Ep. 1, 19, 44</span></i>
			. —<i>Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pŏētĭcē</span></b> , <i>after the manner of poets</i>, <i>poetically</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">loqui (perh. not anteAug., since the words ut
					poëtice loquar,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Fin. 5, 4, 9</span></i>
			, seem not to be genuine), <i><span class="en">Plin. Ep. 8,
				4, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">2, 5,
			5</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">poëtice vel oratorie,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 9, 1, 13</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Lact. 2, 4, 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">3, 14,
			7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Petr.
			90</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pŏētĭca</span></b> ,
			ae, and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pŏētĭcē</span></b> ,
				ēs, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποιητική</span>, <i>the poetic
			art</i>, <i>poetry</i>, <i>poesy</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">o praeclaram emendatricem vitae
					poëticam!</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Tusc. 4, 32, 69</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">1, 1</span></i>
			<i>fin.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">attigit quoque poëticen,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Nep.
					Att. 18, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">a poëtice alienus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					Ep. 7, 4, 2</span></i>
			.</div>
